  "Notes": "Fabry-Perot bandpass at 550 nm, half-wave cavity between quarter-wave mirrors\n\nCaveats:\n- Manufacturability is scored with MINT/MAXT (minimum and maximum layer thickness) at a low weight. A sensitivity term (SENS) would score robustness to thickness errors directly, but it needs second derivatives of the merit function and is not offered; MINT/MAXT keep layers depositable and have exact derivatives.\n- The stop-band rejection asked for here is 0.1%. A real narrowband filter wants optical density 4 or better: use an ODA (optical density) target with a floor for that.",
